  "slug": "the-seam-components-and-the-first-extraction",
  "title": "The seam: components/ and the first extraction",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Create heca/src/components/, fix the contract and the test pattern, and prove both on the highest-frequency composition — the chrome action button.",
  "description": "The folder plus the two rules that decide everything after it, proven on one real extraction rather than asserted in a doc.\n\n## What exists\n\nThere is no `heca/src/components/`. App-level composition lives in `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (4960 lines) and inside providers.\n\nThe **chrome action button** is the highest-frequency inline composition and the best first subject, because AGENTS already documents it as a two-step recipe every caller repeats by hand (AGENTS § \"Chrome buttons → action, tooltip, KeyHint\"):\n\n1. `action_tooltip(button, action_name, label, &state.action_shortcuts)` — `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:521` — composes `\"<label>  <shortcut>\"` from the action's **name**.\n2. `hints.register(InteractionIntent::…)` + `.hint_target(id)` + `.on_click(move || emit(…))` — the same intent registered twice, once for the pick and once for the click.\n\nCall sites doing this by hand include `build_pane_header()` :782 (per configured `PaneAction`, via `pane_action_spec()` :549), `sidebar_toggle_button`, and the overlay's action buttons (`heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs:431`, which already funnels through `action_tooltip`).\n\n## The contract to fix here\n\n- A component takes **plain data plus the app seams it binds** — `Intent` / `ChromeIntentEmitter`, `&mut BuildCx` (drag, hints, signals), an action **name**, a theme. **Never `&AppState`**: it cannot be constructed in a test (it needs a window), so a component that takes it is a component that cannot be tested. Same split that made `route_in_domain`, `cursor_follow` and `resolve_context_for` testable.\n- A component **never** spells a shortcut, picks a glyph, or hardcodes a measure. Name the action; the catalog and `ActionShortcuts` answer.\n- If a proposed component binds **no** app concept, it is a widget in the wrong crate — send it to `heca-grid-ui` instead.\n\n## Test pattern to establish\n\nHeadless, asserting the built tree or the painted scene — not a flag. Follow `heca/src/providers/mod.rs::the_shared_context_carries_nothing_of_one_components_domain` (builds through `ChromeCtx::for_build`, asserts children and what the host registries received) and `heca-grid-ui/tests/phase_a.rs` (paint into a `Scene`, assert `DrawCommand`s). For the action button, assert: the tooltip carries the action's live shortcut, a hint target was registered, and click + pick carry the **same** intent.\n\n## Behaviors to preserve\n\nIdentical pixels; identical hint ids (monotonic, ranges still removed on rebuild); identical tooltip text; the existing `pane_action_spec` mapping of `PaneAction` → (glyph, action, label, focus-first) stays the single source of what a header button is.",
