      "shortName": "heca-src-components-exists-wit",
      "title": "heca/src/components/ exists, with the contract and the test pattern in its module doc",
      "status": "planned",
      "description": "The folder and its rules, before anything moves into it — so the first extraction has something to be correct against.\n\n## What exists\n\nNothing. App-level composition lives in `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs` (4960 lines) and inside providers. `heca/src/main.rs` declares the module list (`mod actions; mod app; mod chrome; …`) — `mod components;` joins it there.\n\n## What to build\n\n`heca/src/components/mod.rs` whose module doc states the contract that the project `globalRules` and AGENTS § 0b define, in the terms of this codebase:\n\n- what may live here (composes widgets **and** binds an app concept: `Intent`, an action **name**, a drag id, a hint target id, a chrome signal, a `nav_key`) versus what belongs in `heca-grid-ui`;\n- the signature rule: plain data + the seams (`Intent` / `ChromeIntentEmitter`, `&mut BuildCx`, an action name, `&GuiTheme`) and **never `&AppState`** — it needs a window, so it cannot exist in a test;\n- what a component returns: a `Component` / `WidgetModel` built from library widgets — no `paint`, no measure, no hit-test, no scroll offset;\n- the test rule: one headless test per component.\n\nNothing else in this task. An empty folder with a written contract is the point; the proof follows in the next task.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- `main.rs` is a binary crate — the module must be reachable from `chrome/` and `providers/` (both already `crate::`-rooted), so plain `pub(crate)` items are enough; nothing here is part of a public API.\n- Do **not** create a `components/` module inside `heca-grid-ui`. The library's own compositions (`Dialog`, `Select`, `CommandPalette`) are widgets and stay where they are.",
